window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-83b3a0cb075beda1"]={"key":"ny_b1-83b3a0cb075beda1","group":"ny_b1","uid":"83b3a0cb075beda1","rank":67,"title":"kestrel heronbank three year coverage roadmap","occupation":"nurse_practitioners","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are Hana Gilchrist, the nurse practitioner preparing Kestrel Clinic's first industrial-client coverage proposal. Heronbank Engineering is adding a permanent night shift at its fabrication yard in January, and Adrien Sandoval, its operations lead, needs a three-year view he can take to the budget committee before committing headcount and a fixed per-employee fee. Use the complete operational records and supplied policy in `heronbank_coverage_inputs.xlsx` as your source, including the injury, referral, staffing, service-boundary, and pricing information. Prepare `heronbank_three_year_coverage_roadmap.docx` and `heronbank_coverage_assumptions.xlsx` in the top level of the working directory, using exactly those filenames. The Word document should be a concise, audience-specific professional report for Adrien: show the proposed coverage by year and shift, the trigger or rationale for each staging decision, the fee and staffing implications, the assumptions behind the projection, and the principal risks or review points. The workbook should make the figures reproducible and should agree with every shared figure in the report. There are two reasonable ways to read the commercial ask: protect the fee that makes the account easy to approve now, or protect the night coverage that remains clinically and operationally credible as demand develops; choose one deliberately, state that choice plainly, and carry it consistently through the recommendation. Adrien has already been told informally that Kestrel will provide 24/7 onsite coverage from January, although the supplied policy places boundaries around what an onsite nurse practitioner service may promise and what must be referred elsewhere. Draw that must-versus-should boundary explicitly rather than quietly treating every request at the yard as an onsite clinical obligation. Do not invent injury volumes, prices, staffing capacity, diagnoses, legal requirements, or guarantees that are not supported by the workbook or policy, and do not present telehealth or referral support as equivalent to onsite care. Keep the report to four pages or fewer, use plain language suitable for a budget committee, identify the assumptions that would change the recommendation, and end with one clear recommendation rather than a list of possible next steps.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/heronbank_coverage_inputs.xlsx` — Complete operational records and the supplied Kestrel Clinic service and pricing policy needed to prepare the three-year coverage roadmap and assumption model.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `heronbank_three_year_coverage_roadmap.docx` — A concise professional report for Adrien Sandoval and Heronbank Engineering's budget committee presenting one three-year onsite health coverage recommendation. (Top level of the working directory; four pages or fewer; must state the chosen commercial priority, show yearly coverage and fee implications, document assumptions and boundaries, and end with one clear recommendation.)\n- `heronbank_coverage_assumptions.xlsx` — A reproducible assumption and projection workbook supporting the figures in the roadmap report. (Top level of the working directory; figures must be traceable to the supplied source and must agree with the report; formulas or clearly documented calculations should expose the projection logic.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/heronbank_coverage_inputs.xlsx","bytes":6523,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/75bf85b970e957da88193865a7f16f6de8aed52c8e5a78620d902908e00e32ec.xlsx","sha256":"75bf85b970e957da88193865a7f16f6de8aed52c8e5a78620d902908e00e32ec","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Coverage Inputs","row_count":25,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["HERONBANK ENGINEERING | KESTREL CLINIC COVERAGE INPUTS","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["Prepared for","Adrien Sandoval, Operations Lead","",""]},{"r":"3","cells":["Source basis","Operational records and Kestrel Clinic policy; complete supplied inputs.","",""]},{"r":"4","cells":["POLICY","Value","Unit / period","Use"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Onsite NP must provide","Scheduled occupational triage, basic assessment within NP scope, first aid, health education, documentation and handoff/referral.","service boundary","permitted onsite work"]},{"r":"6","cells":["Onsite NP must not promise","Emergency response, emergency stabilization, unrestricted diagnosis/treatment, or guaranteed 24/7 physical presence.","service boundary","boundary"]},{"r":"7","cells":["Emergency escalation","Call 911/site emergency response and direct to emergency department; referral or telehealth is not onsite care.","per event","boundary"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Referral handoff","Document disposition and communicate handoff to client contact/external clinician when outside scope.","per event","boundary"]},{"r":"9","cells":["Central telehealth","After-hours telehealth is separate from onsite coverage and cannot be represented as onsite care.","hours/week","service option"]},{"r":"10","cells":["Clinician capacity","1560","onsite hours per NP/year","maximum scheduled onsite"]},{"r":"11","cells":["NP loaded cost","58","USD per onsite hour","staffing cost"]},{"r":"12","cells":["Fixed fee rate","1200","USD per employee/year","client charge"]},{"r":"13","cells":["BASELINE OPERATIONS","Value","Unit / period","Source"]},{"r":"14","cells":["Employees - Year 1","180","employees","headcount plan"]},{"r":"15","cells":["Employees - Year 2","195","employees","headcount plan"]},{"r":"16","cells":["Employees - Year 3","210","employees","headcount plan"]},{"r":"17","cells":["Shift mix at launch","120 day / 40 evening / 20 night","employees","staffing roster"]},{"r":"18","cells":["Injury encounters","24","encounters/year","incident log (12 months)"]},{"r":"19","cells":["Referrals / escalations","8","referrals/year","referral log (12 months)"]},{"r":"20","cells":["After-hours contacts","14","contacts/year","after-hours log"]},{"r":"21","cells":["Night-shift employees - Year 1","20","employees","staffing roster"]},{"r":"22","cells":["Night-shift employees - Year 2","35","employees (scenario)","expansion plan"]},{"r":"23","cells":["Night-shift employees - Year 3","50","employees (scenario)","expansion plan"]},{"r":"24","cells":["Informal commitment","24/7 onsite coverage from January was discussed informally; policy governs contracted scope.","commercial context","reconcile"]},{"r":"27","cells":["Exported 2026-08-20"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/heronbank_coverage_assumptions.xlsx","bytes":8057,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/b8cdd52fc8a889966b4691b6eb3adafc369df96ae9a32c1c27de406026639006.xlsx","sha256":"b8cdd52fc8a889966b4691b6eb3adafc369df96ae9a32c1c27de406026639006","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Source Facts","row_count":14,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["SOURCE FACTS","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["Input","Value","Unit / period","Trace"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Employees Y1","180","employees","headcount plan"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Employees Y2","195","employees","headcount plan"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Employees Y3","210","employees","headcount plan"]},{"r":"6","cells":["Baseline injury encounters","24","encounters/year","incident log"]},{"r":"7","cells":["Baseline referrals","8","referrals/year","referral log"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Baseline after-hours contacts","14","contacts/year","after-hours log"]},{"r":"9","cells":["Night employees Y1","20","employees","staffing roster"]},{"r":"10","cells":["Night employees Y2","35","employees","expansion plan"]},{"r":"11","cells":["Night employees Y3","50","employees","expansion plan"]},{"r":"12","cells":["NP capacity","1560","onsite hours/NP/year","Kestrel policy"]},{"r":"13","cells":["NP loaded cost","58","USD/onsite hour","pricing policy"]},{"r":"14","cells":["Fixed fee rate","1200","USD/employee/year","pricing policy"]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Assumptions","row_count":9,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["SCENARIO ASSUMPTIONS","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["Assumption","Value","Unit / period","Rationale"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Demand growth","0.15","% per year","Planning scenario applied to baseline demand"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Onsite day/evening hours","2600","hours/year","50 scheduled hours/week x 52"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Onsite night hours when activated","2080","hours/year","40 scheduled hours/week x 52"]},{"r":"6","cells":["Telehealth hours Y1/Y2","16","hours/week","Separate after-hours service"]},{"r":"7","cells":["Telehealth hours Y3","24","hours/week","Contingent remote support expansion"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Review trigger","12","night injuries/quarter","Two consecutive quarters reopens schedule/fee"]},{"r":"9","cells":["Rounding rule","1","whole encounter","No double-counting referrals"]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Projection","row_count":14,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["THREE-YEAR COVERAGE PROJECTION","","","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["Metric","Year 1","Year 2","Year 3","Unit","Formula / source"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Employee basis","='Source Facts'!B3  [缓存: 缺失]","='Source Facts'!B4  [缓存: 缺失]","='Source Facts'!B5  [缓存: 缺失]","employees","Source Facts"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Night employees","='Source Facts'!B9  [缓存: 缺失]","='Source Facts'!B10  [缓存: 缺失]","='Source Facts'!B11  [缓存: 缺失]","employees","Source Facts"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Projected injury encounters","=ROUND('Source Facts'!B6,0)  [缓存: 缺失]","=ROUND(B5*(1+'Assumptions'!B3),0)  [缓存: 缺失]","=ROUND(C5*(1+'Assumptions'!B3),0)  [缓存: 缺失]","encounters/year","Baseline x (1 + growth)"]},{"r":"6","cells":["Projected referrals","=ROUND('Source Facts'!B7,0)  [缓存: 缺失]","=ROUND(B6*(1+'Assumptions'!B3),0)  [缓存: 缺失]","=ROUND(C6*(1+'Assumptions'!B3),0)  [缓存: 缺失]","referrals/year","Baseline x (1 + growth)"]},{"r":"7","cells":["Onsite day/evening hours","='Assumptions'!B4  [缓存: 缺失]","='Assumptions'!B4  [缓存: 缺失]","='Assumptions'!B4  [缓存: 缺失]","hours/year","50 h/week x 52"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Onsite night hours","0","='Assumptions'!B5  [缓存: 缺失]","='Assumptions'!B5  [缓存: 缺失]","hours/year","40 h/week x 52 when activated"]},{"r":"9","cells":["Total onsite NP hours","=B7+B8  [缓存: 缺失]","=C7+C8  [缓存: 缺失]","=D7+D8  [缓存: 缺失]","hours/year","day/evening + night"]},{"r":"10","cells":["NPs required","=ROUNDUP(B9/'Source Facts'!B12,0)  [缓存: 缺失]","=ROUNDUP(C9/'Source Facts'!B12,0)  [缓存: 缺失]","=ROUNDUP(D9/'Source Facts'!B12,0)  [缓存: 缺失]","clinicians","hours / 1,560 capacity"]},{"r":"11","cells":["Annual fee","=B3*'Source Facts'!B14  [缓存: 缺失]","=C3*'Source Facts'!B14  [缓存: 缺失]","=D3*'Source Facts'!B14  [缓存: 缺失]","USD/year","employees x $1,200"]},{"r":"12","cells":["Annual staffing cost","=B9*'Source Facts'!B13  [缓存: 缺失]","=C9*'Source Facts'!B13  [缓存: 缺失]","=D9*'Source Facts'!B13  [缓存: 缺失]","USD/year","onsite hours x $58"]},{"r":"13","cells":["Fee less staffing cost","=B11-B12  [缓存: 缺失]","=C11-C12  [缓存: 缺失]","=D11-D12  [缓存: 缺失]","USD/year","fee - staffing cost"]},{"r":"14","cells":["Telehealth availability","='Assumptions'!B6  [缓存: 缺失]","='Assumptions'!B6  [缓存: 缺失]","='Assumptions'!B7  [缓存: 缺失]","hours/week","separate, non-onsite service"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/private/gold/heronbank_three_year_coverage_roadmap.docx","bytes":39018,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/b3c8805f0c69aaa6719b217f842ef8d7feb3b1f79a67ecb11ad54876a9310eaa.docx","sha256":"b3c8805f0c69aaa6719b217f842ef8d7feb3b1f79a67ecb11ad54876a9310eaa","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"HERONBANK ENGINEERING | THREE-YEAR COVERAGE ROADMAP\nPrepared by Hana Gilchrist, Nurse Practitioner, Kestrel Clinic  |  20 August 2026\nDecision in brief\nTo Adrien Sandoval and the Heronbank budget committee: Kestrel should protect credible night coverage as demand develops. The plan schedules weekday night onsite care from Year 2, accepts that the current fixed fee becomes insufficient from that point, and makes any fee reset a documented commercial decision. This is a coverage-sustainability choice, not a promise of unlimited onsite care.\nYear\nPlanned onsite coverage\nAfter-hours telehealth\nOnsite NPs / hours\nFee basis / annual fee\nTrigger / rationale\nYear 1\nDay/evening Mon-Fri, 10 h/day (2,600 h)\n16 h/week; separate\n2 / 2,600 h\n$1,200 x 180 = $216,000\n24 injuries, 8 referrals baseline; night group 20.\nYear 2\nYear 1 plus weekday nights, 8 h/night (4,680 h)\n16 h/week; unchanged\n3 / 4,680 h\n$1,200 x 195 = $234,000\nNight group 35; 15% demand scenario; add NP.\nYear 3\nYear 2 schedule retained; no weekend onsite contracted\n24 h/week; contingent remote\n3 / 4,680 h\n$1,200 x 210 = $252,000\nNight group 50; weekend onsite only if trigger met.\nFinancial and staffing implication\nThe supplied policy caps scheduled onsite work at 1,560 hours per NP per year and prices loaded NP time at $58/hour. Staffing cost is $150,800 in Year 1 (2,600 h), $271,440 in Year 2 (4,680 h), and $271,440 in Year 3. Against the per-employee fee, fee less onsite staffing cost is +$65,200, -$37,440, and -$19,440. The tension becomes material in Year 2, when night hours add 2,080 hours while the fee grows only with headcount. A fee reset or other approved funding is required to sustain the schedule; the recommendation does not hide that consequence.\nService boundary: must vs should refer\nKestrel must provide scheduled occupational triage, basic assessment within NP scope, first aid, work-health education, contemporaneous documentation, and a clear handoff. Kestrel should refer or escalate when outside scope: emergencies go to 911/site emergency response and the emergency department; non-emergency needs go to the appropriate external clinician. Referral and after-hours telehealth support are not onsite care. The NP service does not authorize emergency response, emergency stabilization, unrestricted diagnosis or treatment, or a guarantee of 24/7 physical presence.\nThe informal January message that Kestrel would provide “24/7 onsite coverage” is narrowed by this formal roadmap: weekday night onsite coverage is planned from Year 2, while remote after-hours support and external escalation cover remaining hours. Any broader physical presence requires separately approved scope and fee.\nAssumptions, review points and ownership\nSource facts are the supplied operational records and policy in heronbank_coverage_inputs.xlsx: the launch roster is 120 day, 40 evening and 20 night employees; baseline demand is 24 injury encounters, 8 referrals and 14 after-hours contacts. Deliberate scenario assumptions are 15% annual growth in injury encounters, referrals and after-hours contacts; employee basis 180/195/210; and night employees 20/35/50. Projected demand is rounded to whole encounters and does not double-count referrals as injuries. The workbook exposes each input and formula.\nHana (Kestrel) will report quarterly utilization and handoffs; Adrien (Heronbank) owns roster and budget confirmation. Reassess each quarter-end. If night injury encounters exceed 12 in each of two consecutive quarters, or if two consecutive quarters require more than the modeled 4,680 onsite hours/year run-rate, Adrien and Hana must reopen the night schedule and fee before adding coverage. The principal uncertainty is actual night utilization; changing the 15% growth or night-employee inputs changes hours, clinician count and the fee test.\nRecommendation\nApprove the three-year roadmap as a coverage-sustainability plan: start with 2,600 weekday day/evening onsite hours in Year 1, add 2,080 weekday night hours and a third NP in Year 2, retain that onsite schedule in Year 3, and treat weekend expansion as contingent. Record the current $1,200-per-employee fee as the initial basis and authorize a Year 2 commercial review because the modeled fee no longer covers onsite staffing cost.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report identifies Heronbank Engineering as the client, Kestrel Clinic as the provider, and Adrien Sandoval as the primary audience or decision-maker.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered report text.","grader_hint":"Search the title, opening, or audience statement for all three names and their roles."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report presents a three-year roadmap with distinct coverage decisions for each year.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report roadmap table or equivalent narrative.","grader_hint":"Verify that years one, two, and three are separately identifiable and each has a coverage state."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The roadmap distinguishes onsite coverage, after-hours telehealth, and referral or escalation support rather than treating them as interchangeable services.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report coverage description.","grader_hint":"Check the service matrix or prose for separate labels and distinct availability."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The selected staging is an actual choice with a stated commercial priority: protecting the initial fixed fee or protecting credible night coverage as demand develops.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report recommendation and rationale.","grader_hint":"Accept either priority, but require an explicit choice rather than presenting both as unresolved options."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The chosen priority is carried consistently through staffing, coverage, fee, and recommendation language.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report and workbook.","grader_hint":"Look for contradictions such as claiming to protect the fee while modeling an unacknowledged fee increase or staffing commitment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report acknowledges the informal January 24/7 onsite promise and explains how the formal recommendation handles or narrows that promise.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report scope or risk discussion.","grader_hint":"The promise must be acknowledged and reconciled with policy; silent omission is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report draws a must-versus-should boundary for onsite NP service, including what the service must provide and what it should refer or escalate.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report service-boundary section or matrix.","grader_hint":"Check that the boundary is operationally usable and not merely a generic statement to follow policy."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report does not claim that onsite NP coverage authorizes diagnosis, treatment, emergency response, or other services outside the supplied policy scope.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report scope and limitations.","grader_hint":"Credit only if the report expressly limits unsupported authority or avoids such claims while stating the appropriate referral boundary."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report states that referral or escalation support does not constitute onsite care and identifies the relevant escalation path or limitation from the policy.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report scope language.","grader_hint":"Compare wording against the policy sheet; do not infer equivalence from a general referral mention."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every yearly coverage state is linked to an operational rationale using the supplied injury, referral, or demand records.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report rationale column or narrative and source-linked workbook calculations.","grader_hint":"Each year needs a reason grounded in the input records, not just a generic growth statement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The staging identifies when after-hours telehealth changes, if at all, and when a second clinician is added, if at all, with timing consistent with the selected recommendation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report roadmap and workbook.","grader_hint":"Accept no change where justified, but any change must have a stated timing and source-based rationale."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The model uses the policy's staffing capacity or coverage constraints when determining clinician hours.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook formulas/calculation notes and report assumptions.","grader_hint":"Trace planned hours to the supplied capacity constraint rather than accepting an unsupported staffing number."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Projected demand is derived from the supplied records and stated assumptions rather than invented volumes.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook source and projection calculations.","grader_hint":"Check that baseline volumes and any growth or scenario assumptions are identifiable and source-supported."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook separates source facts from assumptions and calculated outputs.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook labels, formulas, or notes.","grader_hint":"A reviewer should be able to distinguish imported records, user assumptions, and derived figures."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each non-source projection assumption is documented with its value, unit, period, and rationale or source.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook assumption area and report assumption summary.","grader_hint":"Inspect assumptions for explicit units and time basis, not only unlabeled numbers."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The model applies the supplied fixed-fee or per-employee pricing rule correctly to the stated employee basis.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook formulas and policy source.","grader_hint":"Recalculate the fee from the employee basis and applicable policy rate; allow rounding only as documented."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook calculates annual fee revenue or client charge for all three years using the same basis stated in the report.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook projection table and report financial summary.","grader_hint":"Verify all three years and the basis used for the calculation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The model calculates staffing or service cost for all three years from supplied rates or policy inputs and stated hours.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook calculations.","grader_hint":"Trace cost to hours and applicable rate; unsupported cost inputs do not earn credit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report identifies the year or condition in which the fixed-fee and night-coverage tension becomes financially material, using the workbook figures.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report financial discussion and workbook.","grader_hint":"The discussion must identify a specific year or condition and connect it to modeled figures."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recommendation identifies whether the proposed arrangement prioritizes fee stability or coverage sustainability and states the resulting trade-off.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final recommendation.","grader_hint":"Look for an explicit consequence, such as constrained coverage, a fee change, or a review trigger."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report includes at least one measurable review trigger tied to future injury, referral, utilization, staffing, or financial experience.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report monitoring or assumptions section.","grader_hint":"The trigger must be measurable and connected to a decision, not merely 'review regularly.'"},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report states the review timing or cadence for reassessing the roadmap.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report roadmap or review section.","grader_hint":"Accept a quarterly or other explicit cadence if it is operationally coherent."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report identifies the principal uncertainty that could change the recommendation and shows which modeled input would change.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report assumptions or risks.","grader_hint":"Require a concrete input or assumption, not a vague statement that conditions may change."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The roadmap distinguishes planned coverage from contingent coverage and does not present a contingent expansion as already contracted.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report roadmap language.","grader_hint":"Check labels such as planned, contingent, trigger-based, or subject to review."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report preserves the source policy's limitations on emergency care and directs emergencies to the appropriate external response rather than promising onsite management.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report service-boundary language.","grader_hint":"Compare the emergency limitation and direction with the supplied policy."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report preserves the policy's limitations on diagnoses, referrals, or clinical decisions that are not supported by the onsite service.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report scope text.","grader_hint":"Credit a precise limitation paired with the permitted service; generic disclaimers are insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report states what the onsite service must document or communicate at the boundary of care, as required by the supplied policy.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report operating-boundary section.","grader_hint":"Verify the required documentation or handoff duty against the policy source."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook's demand projection reconciles to the supplied baseline records without double-counting the same event or referral.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook source and formulas.","grader_hint":"Reconcile baseline totals to the source records and inspect the counting rule."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook's three-year staffing totals reconcile to the yearly coverage schedule shown in the report.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Both deliverables.","grader_hint":"Compare each year's clinician count and hours, allowing only documented rounding."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook's yearly employee basis and fee figures match the corresponding figures in the report within ±$1 or ±1 employee, as applicable.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Both deliverables.","grader_hint":"Reconcile every shared year-level fee and employee figure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report's stated total or annual financial figures equal the workbook calculations within ±$1 or ±0.1 percentage points where percentages are used.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Both deliverables.","grader_hint":"Recalculate totals from the workbook and compare every figure the report presents as a model output."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook contains visible source, assumptions, and projection content sufficient to audit the model.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook structure and rendered sheets.","grader_hint":"Inspect for clearly labeled content or equivalent auditable organization; do not require a particular sheet count."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Workbook formulas, where used, calculate without broken references, error values, or circular references.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recalculated workbook.","grader_hint":"Open and recalculate with an office-compatible engine or inspect formulas for errors."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report is four pages or fewer when rendered.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX page count.","grader_hint":"Render the document and count pages; do not infer from word count."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A budget committee reader can understand the proposed coverage, financial consequence, and decision without asking the author to decode clinical or modeling jargon.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered report.","grader_hint":"Judge audience fit, plain-language explanations, and whether the central choice is easy to locate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The report is professionally structured and readable, with coherent sequencing from situation and scope through roadmap, assumptions, trade-off, and recommendation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered report.","grader_hint":"Assess whether a busy committee can follow the argument and find the figures without excessive searching."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The final section ends with one clear recommendation rather than unresolved alternatives or a list of next steps.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"End of rendered report.","grader_hint":"Require one selected course of action and no competing recommendation in the closing passage."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report states that its figures and claims are based on the supplied records and policy and identifies any deliberate scenario assumption.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report assumptions or basis statement.","grader_hint":"A source basis and a distinction between fact and scenario assumption must both be visible."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook includes traceable labels or notes linking source-derived inputs to the policy or operational records used.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook labels, notes, or source references.","grader_hint":"Check that a reviewer can identify where each major input came from without guessing."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report includes all material source facts necessary to understand the coverage recommendation, without replacing them with unsupported generalizations.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report compared with supplied workbook.","grader_hint":"Compare the recommendation's factual basis with the source records and policy; focus on material omissions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The roadmap assigns concrete ownership for monitoring demand, reviewing triggers, or approving a coverage change, using roles supported by the source or clearly labeled client/provider roles.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Report governance or review language.","grader_hint":"Accept role-based owners; reject vague statements that someone should monitor the program."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Taken together, the two files are decision-ready: the report can be circulated to the budget committee and the workbook can be used to test the stated assumptions without material ambiguity.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Both rendered deliverables and workbook audit.","grader_hint":"Make an overall professional judgment about completeness, internal consistency, usability, and disciplined clinical claims."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"This is a bounded occupational-health coverage recommendation for one industrial client, combining operational records with a supplied service policy and a three-year scenario model. The audience is a client's budget committee, while the author must preserve clinical scope and avoid unsupported promises.","difficulty_sources":["Choose one defensible three-year coverage staging when the commercial priority is in tension with sustainable night coverage.","Reconcile operational records with policy boundaries and distinguish onsite care from telehealth and referral support.","Model and synthesize a budget-committee-ready report and an auditable assumption workbook with matching figures."],"authoring_plan":{"source_file":{"filename":"heronbank_coverage_inputs.xlsx","purpose":"Create one compact but complete source workbook containing operational records and the only policy text the solver may rely on.","content_requirements":["Include a clearly labeled policy section stating the permitted onsite NP services, the service boundary, emergency escalation requirement, documentation or handoff requirements, and the distinction between onsite care and telehealth or referral support.","Include a baseline operational-record section covering Heronbank employee basis by year or the supplied employee assumption, shift pattern, injury encounters, referral volume, and any other demand measures needed to model three years.","Include deterministic staffing capacity, hourly or annual staffing cost, fee basis, and fixed-fee policy inputs. Keep all figures internally consistent and sufficient to calculate yearly revenue, staffing cost, and the fee-versus-coverage trade-off.","Include a policy or commercial constraint that makes a January 24/7 onsite promise difficult to sustain by year two when night coverage expands. The source should support either defensible reading: preserving fee stability with constrained coverage, or preserving credible night coverage with a stated commercial consequence.","Make the must-versus-should boundary genuinely relevant: for example, the policy may require triage, basic occupational-health assessment, documentation, and referral/escalation, while prohibiting representation of the service as emergency care or unrestricted diagnosis/treatment.","Use synthetic internally consistent records and names only. Do not include real identifiers or addresses."]},"gold_construction":{"method":"Build a reference report and workbook from the source workbook using one internally coherent commercial choice. The selected choice may protect fee stability or coverage sustainability, but it must explicitly state the trade-off and satisfy all policy boundaries.","model_rules":["Baseline demand must reconcile to the supplied operational records without double counting events or referrals.","Three-year demand must be projected from source baseline and explicitly documented assumptions; no unsupported volumes may be introduced.","Yearly onsite hours and clinician count must respect the supplied staffing capacity and the chosen staging.","Telehealth, onsite care, and referral/escalation must remain separate service states.","Annual fee must be calculated from the supplied employee basis and fee rule; annual staffing cost must be calculated from the supplied staffing rate and modeled hours.","All shared annual figures in the report and workbook must match within the rubric tolerances.","The report must acknowledge the informal 24/7 promise, reconcile it with the policy, state the must-versus-should boundary, and avoid claiming emergency authority or unsupported clinical outcomes.","The report must end with exactly one selected recommendation and include a measurable review trigger with an owner and cadence.","The report must be four rendered pages or fewer and readable by a nonclinical budget committee."],"intended_verdict":"A strong submission is a concise doctrinally disciplined recommendation, not a generic clinical overview: it reconciles operational records, models three years, exposes assumptions and arithmetic, makes one deliberate commercial choice, and states both what Kestrel must provide and what it must not promise."},"rubric_coverage":"R01-R04 establish the audience, horizon, roadmap, and deliberate choice. R05-R09 cover the informal promise and clinical must-versus-should boundary. R10-R27 assess professional modeling, policy fidelity, scope limitations, escalation, assumptions, triggers, and the commercial tension. R28-R33 audit reproducibility and cross-file arithmetic. R34-R42 assess format, usability, completeness, ownership, and decision readiness."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"multi_artifact_bundle","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"coverage_inputs","filename":"heronbank_coverage_inputs.xlsx","purpose":"Complete operational records and the supplied Kestrel Clinic service and pricing policy needed to prepare the three-year coverage roadmap and assumption model.","required":true,"discovery":"Use this workbook as the sole factual source; inspect its records and policy text before preparing either deliverable."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"roadmap_report","filename":"heronbank_three_year_coverage_roadmap.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A concise professional report for Adrien Sandoval and Heronbank Engineering's budget committee presenting one three-year onsite health coverage recommendation.","required":true,"constraints":["Top level of the working directory; four pages or fewer; must state the chosen commercial priority, show yearly coverage and fee implications, document assumptions and boundaries, and end with one clear recommendation."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"assumption_workbook","filename":"heronbank_coverage_assumptions.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"A reproducible assumption and projection workbook supporting the figures in the roadmap report.","required":true,"constraints":["Top level of the working directory; figures must be traceable to the supplied source and must agree with the report; formulas or clearly documented calculations should expose the projection logic."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"communicate_stakeholders","work_product":"professional_report","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"professional_judgment"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"nurse_practitioners","sector":"healthcare_social_assistance","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":5.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Have an independent reviewer verify source reconciliation, policy-boundary fidelity, three-year arithmetic, cross-deliverable agreement, page count, and audience usability. Resolve acceptable variation by checking relational predicates rather than literal layout or answer values.","minimum_reviewers":1,"known_limitations":["Either of the two explicitly permitted commercial priorities can be valid if selected deliberately and modeled consistently.","Different professional layouts and equivalent formula structures are acceptable when the figures and policy claims remain auditable."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:41:15+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:41:15+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:41:15+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:41:15+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:41:15+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/83b3a0cb075beda1","declared_deliverables":["heronbank_three_year_coverage_roadmap.docx","heronbank_coverage_assumptions.xlsx"]};
